{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"1a28db6c18e815615f20deb15debfa2a7c14a97303471f00f100ac8c78c65c42","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_0220343532fc80db52f47f996c1c82dd9b5473c79987f6e1b92955c4d5badfba","overall_assessment":"The paper makes a significant theoretical contribution by identifying trajectory length as the underlying mechanism for the exponential dependence of expressivity measures on network depth. This provides a unified framework that connects random network properties to practical training dynamics, offering actionable insights for architectural design and training strategies.","paper_id":"B1TTpYKgx","paper_identity_sha256":"5cf60fd215a2579e0170f5f634815a3e6834f35356dd970e66aa5d43777d0224","prompt_identity_sha256":"fcbbd4c2e3c55320e2c33d438780b079b2f16eb4c87bfbab8cd1f24f353c1ab6","raw_response_sha256":"e13347791d3b132c6733367c820a2eebb225839b2974a4bad1d37d64f9646107","request_identity_sha256":"04bf10be382cf32fa697b52a254db22fa412b6ad3213e2013f718245a9f414c7","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"SIGN","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"22a4924da1c2f5c40ef296ee9f996ea15acd88cb097cbc207fb9bd0920e5a163","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-004","SRC-008","SRC-031"],"review_text":"The work addresses a fundamental question in deep learning: why depth is so effective. By linking three distinct measures of expressivity to a single geometric quantity (trajectory length), the paper provides a unifying theoretical perspective that is likely to influence research in network architecture, optimization, and generalization. The finding that early layers have a disproportionate influence on expressivity is a broad insight that can inform various subfields, from initialization schemes to curriculum learning.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-BRD"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-002","SRC-024","SRC-026"],"review_text":"The paper demonstrates domain relevance by applying its theoretical findings to standard computer vision benchmarks (MNIST and CIFAR-10). The experiments show that training earlier layers leads to better performance, a practical takeaway for practitioners designing deep networks. However, the domain impact is somewhat limited by the use of simple, fully-connected architectures and small-scale datasets, which may not fully capture the complexities of modern, large-scale deep learning applications.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-DOM"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-005","SRC-008","SRC-014"],"review_text":"The paper improves upon the state of the art by moving beyond the 'hardcoded' weight comparisons and unrealistic architectural assumptions of prior expressivity work. It provides a rigorous theoretical bound (Theorem 1) on the growth of trajectory length and empirically verifies the exponential dependence of expressivity measures on depth. This represents a substantial advance in understanding the theoretical underpinnings of deep network performance, offering a more general and principled approach than previous studies.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-SOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-031"],"review_text":"The paper suggests that its findings could inform practical training strategies, such as new pre-training or initialization schemes, and rules for early stopping. By understanding the trade-off between stability and expressivity during training, practitioners may be able to design more efficient and robust training pipelines. However, the paper does not explicitly discuss broader societal impacts or risks, focusing instead on the technical and theoretical contributions.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"083a0679e8e98e2bdc9f8b31cd47840f4ebe6739cd336614000e622f049ff029","paper_id":"B1TTpYKgx","paper_ordinal":11,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"e13347791d3b132c6733367c820a2eebb225839b2974a4bad1d37d64f9646107","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1TTpYKgx","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"181a3e91f622d47d059188bfca4eca03d8415dc51634dea88cd730daa4b49954","request_identity_sha256":"04bf10be382cf32fa697b52a254db22fa412b6ad3213e2013f718245a9f414c7","role":"SIGN","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":670,"prompt_tokens":16472,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":17142},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"04bf10be382cf32fa697b52a254db22fa412b6ad3213e2013f718245a9f414c7","role":"SIGN","role_ordinal":2,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}